  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Restoration of Livestock Services in Conflict and Drought Affected Areas of Ethiopia (RESTORE)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;The project is in line with the frameworks of IM3 component 2 that aims to &lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;support sustainable recovery of the livestock system&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; in response to the conflict and drought induced crises, and increase overall sector productivity and improve the marketing of livestock products in &lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Tigray, Afar and South Easter Ethiopia regional states.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; The planned interventions include, among others: 1) &lt;em&gt;improving the quality and reliability of integrated public and private veterinary service delivery; 2) support the Federal MoA in the improvement of compliance and enforcement of animal health, food safety standards, responding to market requirements; 3) availability and quality of livestock feeds through farmers/pastoralists -private sector driven fodder production and marketing, and 4) enhance leather value chain development through supporting of skin and hide processing systems&lt;/em&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</narrative>
  </description>
